WEBVTT

00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:13,500
Why would somebody with cancer have anemia?

00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,140
So in anemia, there's different types of anemia.

00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:23,900
So you could have anemia due to blood loss.

00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,980
You can see that in a person with cancer.

00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:29,540
If the person has, especially if they have a cancer

00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:32,860
in the intestinal tract and they're having bleeding,

00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:35,420
then they have blood loss.

00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:38,820
Or you have a vaginal cancer, a uterine cancer,

00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:40,660
where you have blood loss.

00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:45,900
You could have anemia due to a loss of blood.

00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:48,380
So let's say a person doesn't have cancer

00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:50,340
and they go in for a regular physical

00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:52,540
and they have low red blood cell comb

00:00:52,540 --> 00:00:54,220
to some other signs of anemia,

00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,300
the red cell width and things like that.

00:00:57,780 --> 00:00:59,140
The first thing that doctors should do

00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:03,620
is try to investigate what is the cause of this anemia.

00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:08,060
But if a person already has a diagnosis of cancer

00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:11,860
and now their hemoglobin is going down

00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:14,300
to their red blood cell count is going down.

00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:19,300
Their red cell width is going up things like that.

00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:24,820
Other signs of anemia of chronic disease,

00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:27,020
that's a different type of anemia.

00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:30,220
So anemia of chronic disease is actually the name

00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:33,540
of a type of anemia that's very often,

00:01:33,580 --> 00:01:35,660
very common in cancer,

00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:38,340
especially later stage cancer,

00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:41,580
it's common for a couple of reasons.

00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:45,260
Number one, if the person is doing chemotherapy,

00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:49,180
chemotherapy can affect red blood cell production

00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:52,500
and cause anemia of chronic disease.

00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:55,060
If the person is not doing chemotherapy,

00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:58,540
another reason why you can get anemia of chronic disease

00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:02,860
with cancer is because of a general state of inflammation.

00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:09,460
Inflammation, especially that affects red blood cell

00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:13,180
production is not uncommon and that can be a cause.

00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:18,140
Another cause can be the cancer is godly up iron.

00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:20,740
Iron can be a fuel source for cancer

00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:23,380
that can be one of the issues.

00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:27,540
And that is kind of a, becomes problematic

00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:30,700
because typically if a person has iron deficiency

00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:33,460
in anemia, what has to do with blood loss,

00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:35,660
you'd give the person iron

00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:37,700
and you can't give the person,

00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:40,220
or you have to be careful giving a cancer patient iron

00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:41,780
because it can be feeding the cancer.

00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:43,660
So that's why you would always use that iron

00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,900
or an revisited protocol if you're going to do that.

00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:48,660
So you'd add an revisited with the iron

00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:53,220
if you do want to supplement iron.

00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:56,740
Another side note of this, if a person has elevated ferritid,

00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:59,220
even if they have anemia, you can't give them iron.

00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:01,860
So if you have elevated ferritid and you give iron,

00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:04,500
you're going to make the person worse.

00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:08,660
Elevated ferritid is a side of heavy inflammation

00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:10,740
and you have to be careful with that.

00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:15,380
So there's multiple reasons why you'd get anemia with cancer.

00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:17,740
You have to investigate all of those.

00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:22,740
We've had questions on this forum in the past,

00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:27,300
multiple times whether a person should get a blood transfusion

00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:29,420
if they have anemia.

00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:31,860
That's quite severe and the answer has been,

00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:36,380
well, typically they will give you one every hospital,

00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:40,140
every clinic has their cutoff range.

00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:44,700
Usually you have to have a hemoglobin below 8.0.

00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:48,500
Some of it, some people, some clinics, it's below 7.5.

00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:50,820
Some it's you have to be down to 7.0 before

00:03:50,820 --> 00:03:52,900
they'll give you a transfusion.

00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:57,500
And my answer is always, yes, I think it's in the best interest

00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:00,780
to get that, it can really help you feel better.

